last bit shocked you just now you should  totally check out my previous theory on  the goddess statues anyway  hylia as a goddess being or even just an  idea was not present in zelda lore until  the release of skyward sword  not even kidding for such an immensely  important member of zelda lore it's  interesting to think about the fact that  we've only known of her existence  since skyward sword so for only the past  10 years  even though breath of the wild is the  game that takes place the furthest from  skyward sword in the timeline  to us the players it was the game that  was released right after  and lo and behold the goddess hylia is  not only present in the game but  is literally everywhere you can't go to  any town in the game without seeing the  physical representation of skyward  sword's direct  inspiration and what's more is the  goddess statues and shrines are even  constructed exactly like they were in  skyward sword in fact the entire setting  for breath of the wild is extremely  similar to skyward swords because  as we know skyward sword tells the story  of the beginning of the franchise and if  you'll recall one of the first things  you hear in breath of the wild is that  the great plateau  is the birthplace of all of hyrule but  i'm getting carried away with this at  this point if you'd like a more in-depth  look at the comparison between the  related areas of the two games i  recommend this video by rmfh  and hey tell him i sent you secondly the  talking master sword was also taken  directly from skyward sword you see  the master sword has for a long time  been theorized as having some sort of  sentience to it as in twilight princess  for instance midna states that the sword  chose link as its master instead of link  choosing the sword  interesting choice of words that for a  long time was unresolved and left up to  speculations  until skyward sword that is if you  haven't played it you might not have  heard of the individual in the game  whose name i still cannot get a straight  answer on how it's pronounced  wow i can literally hear you typing out  her pronunciation in the comments below  huh you guys are funny phi or fee as  some call her  is revealed in skyward sword to be the  sentience in the goddess sword which  later on becomes the one and only master  sword well unless there's actually two  of them but  anyway she serves as link's companion  throughout his adventure and lets him  know  every time the batteries in his wiimote  are running low yeah anyway the point is  that phi  is a being that lives inside of the  master sword and for all intents and  purposes  actually is the master sword in breath  of the wild we see the master sword  speaking to zelda while this is already  enough to point towards a skyward sword  inspiration  the developers took it one step further  and actually put the same  little musical tone in the game that  plays whenever fee speaks to you in  skyward sword  take a  the listen so he can't  yup there you have it the second  straight up 100  bonafide skyward swordism thirdly and  most obviously  parkour and stamina but let's face it  mostly parkour  you see one of the most ground-breaking  things about breath of the wild that  separates it from other open world games  is the fact that  link here can literally climb anything  except for smooth surfaces apparently  but for some reason i find that one  difficult to explain since while he  can't climb the surfaces of sheikah  shrines he can instead climb the  completely smooth walls of gerudo town  either way link's parkour initiatives  originated in skyward sword where he  could sprint at a wall and take a solid  two steps directly upwards like this was  legend of assassin's skyward creed  this was the first time in any zelda  game where you were able to even  slightly parkour much less sprint as  link and the longer you sprinted or did  anything requiring physical exertion the  more stamina you used and thus  nintendo invented the wheel the stamina  wheel  look familiar because it basically  functions the exact same way in breath  of the wild  you sprint or climb or even hit hard and  you spend stamina  now one thing that breath of the wild  improved upon was the fact that you  could actually level up your stamina  wheel by way of the spirit orbs gained  from shrines either way though it's  interesting to think back upon the fact  that we can  literally see the roots of this very key  and well-known in-game mechanic  fourthly crafting now this is an in-game  mechanic that's super popular in the  open world genre already  but in terms of breath of the wild it  was completely absent from zelda games  until skyward sword  in the game crafting was used to upgrade  your equipment and gear at the gear shop  in the bazaar and even craft things like  potions at the potion shop  in breath of the wild this concept  evolved into three things  cooking the great fairies and the  sheikah scientist duo  cooking of course covers the creation of  potions and elixirs like the previous  game but also  most obviously had the added ability to  create you know  cooked food the great fairies replaced  the old bizarre upgrades by allowing you  to gather materials and enhance the  armor you wear  and pura slash robbie will either  upgrade your runes which replace  tools or craft gear from the sheikh  materials one thing that breath of the  wild did not change from skyward swords  crafting is the fact that link can't  just  up and craft something by himself  similar to the shopkeepers in the bazaar  link still needs to go visit the sheikah  duo the great fairies or a pod over an  open flame to craft whatever his  hearts desire fifthly and most  importantly the sail cloth i mean  paraglider  the paracloth was a concept taken  directly from skyward sword since one of  the main aspects of the game is quite  literally falling from the sky it's a  pretty decent death preventing measure  to take when doing such an action mr  onuma specifically mentioned this in the  previous nintendo direct when he was  talking about breath of the wild skyward  sword inspirations as well  they did improve the sail glider's  functionality by allowing link to glide  with it instead of just  fall slowly but the fact remains that  the concept of gliding to reach areas  previously unreachable 100 came from  skyward sword and that's the list anyway  guys thank you so much for watching and  i hope that if you haven't played the  game before or in a while  you found this interesting let me know  if you learned something new or if i  forgot something in the comments below  please be sure to leave a like if you  enjoyed the video so that this gets  spread around to others and helps hype  up skyward sword's release  also subscribe if you haven't already  for much more nintendo content to come  as always huge huge huge thanks to my  amazing supporters who are literally the  people that make all of this possible  please give a huge welcome to a new  bandit level supporter of mine the skull  kid nico  and the two new faces of x superfish and  not so heroic link who have all decided  to join my elite bandit crew  thank you guys so much and if you  watching are interested in joining said  crew and helping the next videos come to  life  please feel free to check out that join  button located below or find the link to  my patreon in the description below  also down there is a link to my merch  website where i've just gone live with  some truly snazzy new  bandit coin or boin related merch  even if you can't support monthly you  can still join the bandit crew by  picking up just one of these cute little  merch items  and trust me it is so incredibly  appreciated that's all i've got for you  in this one so as always i hope you have  a wonderful rest of your day  this is masentana bandit signing out  [Music]  you

